    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole test is `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature in the Spring PetClinic REST app. The household **duplicate-rejection** and `sharesHousehold` opt-in logic already existed; the missing piece was assigning and returning a stable shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto`.\n\n3. **`v1/HouseholdNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added `householdId(lastName, address)`, which derives a stable, opaque identifier (first 16 hex chars of SHA-256) purely from the **normalized** last name + address. Because it reuses the same normalization as the existing `sameHousehold` match, any two owners that share a household deterministically derive the *same* id \u2014 no cross-owner state coordination needed.\n\n4. **`v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Assigns `owner.setHouseholdId(...)` on create. Every owner in a given household gets the same value, so joiners created with `sharesHousehold=true` share one identifier, which is returned in the response and via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n5. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and appended the matching `NULL` to the positional owner inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the one the tests use).\n\nThe new `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` acceptance test \u2014 which creates two owners sharing a first owner's last name + address with `sharesHousehold=true` and asserts they return an identical, non-blank `householdId` \u2014 now passes, and so does the full suite.\n\nNote: the `mysql`/`postgres`/`h2` seed data was already out of sync with its own schema before this change (e.g. the mysql owners inserts predate `customer_code`) and isn't exercised by tests, so I left those seeds alone rather than fix pre-existing unrelated drift \u2014 happy to bring them into sync if you'd like.",
